# Coding conventions (enforce on every change)

**Sources:** `.docs/coding-conventions.md`, `.docs/folder-structure.md`, `.docs/screen-standard.md`, `eslint.config.js`.  
Treat these as hard requirements — PR review and ESLint will catch slips.

---

## 1. Component / file structure

**Two layouts — pick by reuse scope:**

### Shared kit (`src/components/{elements,form,ui}/`)

- Folder + primary file: **kebab-case** (`my-date-picker/my-date-picker.tsx`).
- **`index.ts(x)` = re-export only** — no component implementation in `index`.
- Co-locate per component folder:
  - **`type.ts`** — all `interface` / `type` / props (never export types from `.tsx`)
  - **`styles.ts`** — `generateStyles(theme)` + `useThemedStyles` (never `StyleSheet.create` / `generateStyles` inside `.tsx`)
  - **`hooks.ts`** — optional
- Product variants in the same kit folder may use `*.styles.ts` (e.g. `private-sidebar.styles.ts`).

```
my-foo/
  my-foo.tsx
  index.ts       # re-export only
  type.ts
  styles.ts
  hooks.ts       # optional
```

### Feature-only UI (`src/features/<feature>/components/`)

UI used **only** by that feature (do **not** put these in `src/components/ui`).

- **Flat**: one `.tsx` file per component — **no** nested folder + `index` / `styles` / `type` per component.
- Shared **`styles.ts`** + **`type.ts`** in that `components/` folder (or reuse screen `styles.ts`).
- Screens stay thin; large presentational blocks live here.

```
src/features/<feature>/components/
  styles.ts
  type.ts
  order-summary-card.tsx
  status-badge.tsx
```

- Imports: alias `@/*` only.

---

## 2. Styles & theme

- **No inline styles** (`style={{ … }}`) — ESLint `react-native/no-inline-styles`. Exception: values that must be computed from props/state/layout (e.g. measured width). Prefer named styles in `styles.ts`.
- Colors / spacing / radius / typography: theme tokens (`getColor`, `getSpacing`, `getRadius`, …).
- Borders: `border/…` tokens — no hardcoded hex / `brand/black` as border.
- Shadows: `MySurface` + `elevation="soft/…"` — no raw `shadowColor` / numeric `elevation` in StyleSheet.
- Screen background: `fill/background/primary` (not `brand/white` — breaks dark mode).

---

## 3. My* kit before RN primitives

| Avoid | Prefer |
|-------|--------|
| `View` | `MyView` (except thin glue / implementing MyView) |
| `Text` | `MyText` |
| URL `Image` | `MyImage` (fullscreen gallery → `ImagePreview`) |
| Press / button / icon / input / sheet / spinner | `MyPressable`, `MyButton`, `MyIcon`, `MyTextInput`, `MyBottomSheet`, `MySpinner`, `MySurface` |
| Card / divider / search | `MyCard`, `MyDivider`, `MySearchInput` |
| Empty / error / skeleton | `MyEmptyState`, `MyErrorState`, `MySkeleton` |

- Prefer **ContainerStyleProps** (`margin`, `padding`, `gap`, …) on My* over stuffing layout into `style`.
- Do not wrap a single child in an extra `View`/`MyView` with no layout purpose.
- Catalog: `.docs/shared-ui-catalog.md`.

---

## 4. Handlers & lists

- **No new arrow functions in JSX:** `onPress={() => …}`, `renderItem={({ item }) => …}`.
- Use `useCallback` / named functions; OK to pass `setState` setters directly.
- Exceptions: Reanimated worklets; `setState(prev => …)` inside a callback (not inline in JSX).
- **List `key`:** do not use bare `key={item.id}`. Use a stable prefixed key, e.g. `` key={`drawer-item-${item.id}`} ``, `` key={`sidebar-footer-${item.id}`} ``.

---

## 5. Null / equality / platform

- No `!= null` / `== null`. Use `isNil` / `!isNil` from `lodash`.
- ESLint `eqeqeq: always` — use `===` / `!==`.
- Distinguish null vs undefined only when needed: `=== null` / `=== undefined`.
- Platform flags: `isWeb` / `isIos` / `isAndroid` from `@/constants/dimensions` — avoid `Platform.OS === 'web'` in UI when helpers exist.
- **Layout breakpoints:** `useIsMobileSize()` / `isMobileSize` — never use `Platform.OS` to decide mobile vs desktop layout.
- `Platform.OS` only for true platform APIs (native modules, permissions, picker engines).

---

## 6. App / feature / screen placement

- `src/app` = **thin route shell** only (layouts, redirects, `export { default } from '@/features/…'`).
- No API calls, business logic, or large screen UI inside `src/app` route files.
- Authenticated chrome lives in **`(private)/_layout`** — do **not** invent `(shell)` or `features/shell`.
- Production screens: `features/<feature>/screens/` with **container + view + styles** (+ optional `use-*.ts` / types). See `.docs/screen-standard.md`.
- Do not copy playground screen structure into production features.

---

## 7. Conditional UI & sheets

- Prefer `ConditionRenderer` when there is a clear `when` + `fallback`.
- `MyTextInput` inside `MyBottomSheet` → must use `useBottomSheetTextInput`.

---

## 8. Align with ESLint / Prettier (do not fight the linter)

From `eslint.config.js`:

- Prettier: no semicolons, single quotes, trailing commas, printWidth 100.
- `unused-imports`: remove unused imports/vars (prefix intentional unused with `_`).
- `prefer-const`, `curly: all`, `eqeqeq`.
- `no-console` except `console.warn` / `console.error`.
- `no-debugger`: error.
- Run / respect `yarn lint` — fix errors before considering the task done.

---

## 9. Data / async (short)

- API contracts via RTK `createApi`; thunks for multi-step orchestration; slice reducers stay pure sync.
- Details: `.docs/data-state-standard.md`.

---

## 10. Scope & git

- DRY: shared logic/UI in 2+ places → extract.
- Do not edit outside the task; no unsolicited markdown/docs.
- Branch names: `feat/` | `fix/` | `issue/` | `release/` — not `cursor/`.

---

## Pre-merge checklist (UI)

- [ ] Shared kit: types in `type.ts`; `index` re-export only; styles in `styles.ts`
- [ ] Feature-only: flat `components/*.tsx` + shared `components/styles.ts` / `type.ts`
- [ ] No inline style / inline JSX handlers
- [ ] Prefixed list keys
- [ ] My* + theme tokens; `isWeb`/`isNil`/`useIsMobileSize` as applicable
- [ ] Thin `app/` routes; screens under `features/…/screens`
- [ ] Lint clean (errors fixed)
